; DECLARATION PRELUDE — consumed via `babylon_bsl::scenario::
; load_scenario_with_prelude` (Train B item 4, issue #591, D157 —
; docs/reference/bsl-language.rst §2.13). NOT a scenario: no
; `(scenario <qname> ...)` wrapper, and only the four declaration top-forms
; are legal here (`defenum` / `defvocabulary` / `defconst` / `deffield`) —
; a prelude declares, it never seeds a graph.
;
; The WorldView mint (ADR206), DUPLICATING the mint scenario's own
; declaration (worldview-foundation.bscn:34's `(defenum WorldView ...)`
; still stands — nothing was factored out of it) so a consuming scenario
; can resolve `WorldView`-typed fields WITHOUT re-declaring the type
; itself. A scenario MAY still re-declare it verbatim (`EnumRegistry::
; declare`'s identical-recognition arm resolves to the SAME id, this
; train); a scenario that declares it differently still refuses, exactly
; as any other conflicting `defenum` does.
;
; Member order is RULED content (design doc §4.1, Director-approved
; 2026-08-14): REVOLUTIONARY / LIBERAL / FASCIST. Declaration order IS the
; storage ordinal (ADR195), so the ruled order makes REVOLUTIONARY=0,
; LIBERAL=1, FASCIST=2 — the same declared TEXT as worldview-foundation
; .bscn's own declaration (this file's form sits at column 0; the mint's
; sits indented two spaces inside its `(scenario ...)` form, so the LINE
; bytes differ even though the declaration itself does not). The ordinal
; claim is enforced executably by `tick_goldens.rs`'s
; `worldview_prelude_member_order_is_the_ruled_ordinal`, not by this
; comment (final whole-branch review, 2026-08-17, item 2).
(defenum WorldView (REVOLUTIONARY LIBERAL FASCIST))
